{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5d0c02ef-0611-4ae7-89f4-53bec055c070","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have run the read-only MCP checkup against [server.py](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py) on port `52749` and written the full report to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/ANSWER.md) without modifying any server files.\n\n### Summary of Findings (`has the problem`)\n\n1. **What applied from your colleague's note:**\n   - The read-only Streamable HTTP checkup protocol and checks **C1–C10** (except the external MCP Registry lookup in **C6**, since [README.md](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/README.md#L14) notes the server is not yet listed in any registry).\n   - The colleague's preamble observation—that a server advertises `resources` in `initialize` and then responds to `resources/list` with `401`—applies directly to [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L135-L155).\n   - External worklore reporting and the `incomplete` rule for auth-gated read tools did not apply.\n\n2. **Failures in the 10-check table:**\n   - **C2 (FAIL):** [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L113-L119) / [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L161-L164) turns missing required arguments (`get_note({})`) and nonexistent IDs (`get_note({\"id\": \"n-999\"})`) into JSON-RPC `-32602` protocol errors instead of tool results with `isError: true`, causing client SDKs to throw. Meanwhile, `search_notes({})` ignores its required `query` parameter completely and returns all notes.\n   - **C5 (FAIL):** In [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L112) for `search_notes`, `content[0].text` is serialized as a bare JSON array (`hits`), while `structuredContent` is an object (`{\"hits\": hits, \"total\": len(hits)}`).\n   - **C6 (FAIL / WARN):** No surface lock file or test exists in the repository to ensure `serverInfo.version` (`0.3.1`) moves when the surface hash (`sha256:4fe710618f54d5e6c4bea883aea0cd891d8f8284345432b6d7e3039dbd1ec505`) changes.\n   - **C10 (FAIL):** `search_notes` declares a vacuous [`outputSchema`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L34) (`{\"type\": \"object\"}`) with no required fields or value constraints, accepting corrupted output (`{}`).\n   - **C1, C3, C4, C7, C8, C9 (PASS):** Open `initialize` / `tools/list` / `server/discover`, session survival across errors, valid calls matching `outputSchema`, per-call JSON stderr logging via [`log`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L80-L83), valid tool names (`^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`), and honest version negotiation on `\"protocolVersion\": \"banana\"` all passed.\n\n3. **Additional real-client pitfalls documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/ANSWER.md):**\n   - `initialize` advertises `capabilities.resources`, but [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L148-L150) returns HTTP `401` on `resources/list` without a token, even though `notes://guide` is a static usage guide.\n   - `resources/read` ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L155)) ignores `params.get(\"uri\")`.\n   - Calling `add_note` with a valid token but missing `title` or `body` raises an uncaught `KeyError` ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L126)), dropping the connection.\n   - Client notifications other than `notifications/initialized` receive a `-32601` JSON-RPC error response ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L168)), and JSON-RPC batch requests ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L205-L211)) bypass [`log`](file:///tmp/h-yajJEq/server.py#L216) and session handling.\n","duration_seconds":384.430001,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":58540,"output_tokens":28999,"thinking_tokens":17922,"cache_read_tokens":254407,"total_tokens":87539}}}
